(3464040, 482528, 65886, '<td valign="top">why when we think about time we often think about something technical? mechanical? maybe because mechanical things go almost "always" and their stability reflects the stability of time? and we are also used to think about time as dots, as punktum, as something 1-2-3, boom-boom-boom, strikes, and not the continuum. quite interesting, isn''t it?</td>', 'why when we think about time we often think about something technical? mechanical? maybe because mechanical things go almost "always" and their stability reflects the stability of time? and we are also used to think about time as dots, as punktum, as something 1-2-3, boom-boom-boom, strikes, and not the continuum. quite interesting, isn''t it?', '2007-03-15 12:49:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(3464046, 482279, 65886, '<td valign="top">yay!!! you''d better get a ribbon with this one :P<br/>cool idea, very symbolic, cool with this white background, much much better than it could have been in a "real" prison with a brick wall and stuff. good luck:)</td>', 'yay!!! you''d better get a ribbon with this one :Pcool idea, very symbolic, cool with this white background, much much better than it could have been in a "real" prison with a brick wall and stuff. good luck:)', '2007-03-15 12:50:26.000000', NULL, 1),
